from mkchar import mk

mk("Amos_Pensinata.md", "Amos Pensinata", "2", "Book 7", "Book 11", "Books 7, 9, 10, 11 (chapter files)",
   "Jason_Asano.md, Dawn.md, ../03_Magic_and_Adventuring/Auras.md",
   "A gold-rank adventurer with a soul-damaged aura who teaches Jason aura and soul techniques and is lost to an orb in Cardinas.",
   ["Trenchant asks whether anyone has worked with Amos Pensinata (Book 7, Ch44 L30). Dawn names him as a gold-ranker whose experiences with soul trauma left him with a more capable aura than most; she has convinced him to travel with Jason to teach soul manipulation (Book 9, Ch6 L47).",
    "Jason knows him by reputation as the man who defeated the same forces that had forced Jason to flee the underwater complex (Book 9, Ch6 L48).",
    "Jason later learns from him how to combine auras into a single force (Book 9, Ch94 L30) and about controlling aspects of the soul in isolation, which helped him expand perception without a beacon-like aura (Book 10, Ch28 L7).",
    "Clive turns on him at the Yaresh camp: \"You were brought on to help Jason, not make things worse. But your baggage...\" (Book 9, Ch42 L90).",
    "He debriefs a Rimaros team in Cardinas (Book 10, Ch64 L9) and is among the few able to resist the zone's corruption (Book 11, Ch47 L64).",
    "In Book 11 he does not flee with the other gold-rankers but goes into the water orb (Book 11, Ch54 L18-21), and Jason promises to try to get him back (Book 11, Ch54 L56).",
    "Orin Pensinata is named in Book 9 as leading a team that stays outside while others go below (Book 9, Ch24 L48); no relation is stated in the lines checked."],
   "Calm and wry, with a teacher's patience and a soldier's scars.",
   open_q=["His fate after entering the orb (Book 11, Ch54) and his relation to Orin Pensinata."])

mk("Hannah_and_Claire_Adeah.md", "Hannah and Claire Adeah", "1", "Book 1", "Book 13", "Books 1, 2, 10, 13 (chapter files)",
   "Rick_Geller.md, Dustin_Kettering.md, ../06_Places/Greenstone.md",
   "Twin elf sisters on Rick Geller's team: Hannah the archer and Claire the healer.",
   ["The elf twins Hannah and Claire Adeah are the archer and the team healer, with Claire the most important member to protect (Book 1, Ch67 L15; Book 2, Ch29 L6-8).",
    "Hannah's arrows pin trap weavers and she has \"the best eyes\" (Book 1, Ch67 L18-33); Claire cleanses afflictions and cuts a team mate from a web with her wand (Book 1, Ch66 L31; Book 1, Ch67 L71-95).",
    "In the Book 1 mock battle Jason takes Claire down first, and her body floats in the water while the others vow revenge (Book 1, Ch67 L126-128).",
    "Claire resented Jason's tactics in the mock battle the most (Book 2, Ch4 L10).",
    "By Book 10 Hannah is Rick's girlfriend and then fiancée (Book 10, Ch1 L77-80; Book 10, Ch51 L3); by Book 12 his wife (Book 12, Ch15 L6).",
    "In Book 13 Claire Adeah is on the expedition with Arabelle and Sigrid and says the vampires have too much magic for the cure to be safe (Book 13, Ch958 L39, L61). (A different Claire, Claire Davney, is the US Secretary of State, Book 13, Ch963 L24.)"],
   "Hannah is wry and physical (she kicks Rick's shin, Book 10, Ch51 L9); Claire is blunt and the healer's voice of caution.")

mk("Audrey_Blaine.md", "Audrey Blaine", "3", "Book 5", "Book 13", "Books 5, 13 (chapter files)",
   "Mr_North.md, Elizabeth.md, ../05_Organisations/Earth_Powers.md",
   "A Network committee member (\"Mrs South\") who survives a failed secret programme in a cloned body and later directs the Asano clan's energy-vampire research.",
   ["In Book 5 Mrs South, named Audrey, is pressed by Mr North and Mrs West to go along with them (Book 5, Ch8 L63-65).",
    "She wakes in a new body that had been in stasis for more than a dozen years, the last remnant of a secret programme whose progenitors she had killed (Book 5, Ch10 L17-33).",
    "The new body was cloned from her own DNA with Cabal biological material (Book 5, Ch10 L24).",
    "In Book 13 Jason introduces Audrey Blaine to Team Biscuit as having run a sketchy joint programme between the magical factions decades ago, the source of her current state, which she has learned to manage (Book 13, Ch959 L60); she has lived in a magic city for a decade among vampires (Book 13, Ch959 L50).",
    "The Asano clan snatched her from the Network as a coup (Book 13, Ch987 L10) and she is the clan's energy-vampire research director (Book 13, Ch992 L116; Book 13, Ch998 L109)."],
   "Dry, practical and unsentimental; she has lived with the consequences of her own research.")

